+## Real CLI review application (helper 0.10.2)
+
+A refreshed review export is not proof its exact bytes have been applied.
+Before headline preparation the canonical helper explicitly applies that export
+through `clip review --apply` with the same disposable combined profile. It never
+forges a digest or bypasses approval. The stricter fixture changes refreshed
+bytes and refuses preparation until those exact bytes are applied. Both doctor
+checks, private content receipts and caption/music/closing cleanup remain.
+Install the pinned Linux prerequisite patch/model from the Core installer for
+Linux shots rendering; no fallback to blurred fit. Template framing reserves
+headroom for the whole camera shot using measured face bounds and the existing
+zoom cap. Impossible headroom fails explicitly, and legacy framing is unchanged.
+Content-free CLI failures expose only finite HEADLINE layout/face/asset codes,
+so the helper need not capture private stderr to show actionable failures.
+These changes do not restart a production worker or publish any clips.
+
